              "exam_name": "NEET 2017 · NCERT",
              "question": "<p>A physical quantity of the dimensions of length that can be formed out of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(c, G,~\\text{and}~\\dfrac{e^2}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0}\\)</span>is:<br>(<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(c\\)</span> is the velocity of light, <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(G\\)</span> is the universal constant of gravitation and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(e\\)</span> is charge)</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:500px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(c^2\\left[G \\dfrac{e^2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\right]^{\\dfrac{1}{2}}\\)</span></td><td>2.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\dfrac{1}{c^2}\\left[\\dfrac{e^2}{4 G \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\right]^{\\dfrac{1}{2}}\\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\dfrac{1}{c} G \\dfrac{e^2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\)</span></td><td>4.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\dfrac{1}{c^2}\\left[G \\dfrac{e^2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\right]^{\\dfrac{1}{2}}\\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>",
